<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The photo of Silicon Valley centi-billiona=
ires at Donald Trump=E2=80=99s inauguration =E2=80=93 Musk, Bezos, and Zuck=
erberg, front row and side by side =E2=80=93 now looks like a hitlist for a=
 blue Congress hellbent on making life difficult for billionaires.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The picture symbolized at the time the ben=
ding of the knee by the richest men in the world to its most powerful, a sy=
mbiosis of the ultra-rich. Already unfathomably wealthy, Silicon Valley tyc=
oons believed a Maga-sized public shift to the right would enrich them even=
 more. It did. For several years, while Trump seemed an everlasting kingmak=
er and AI=E2=80=99s expansion seemed unstoppable, their fortunes ballooned =
to values beyond comprehension. Elon Musk=E2=80=99s surpassed $1tn.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In the harsh blue light of Tuesday=E2=80=
=99s midterms, though, going all-in on Maga seems an unwisely unhedged bet.=
 Democrats took decisive control of the US Congress, flipping seats right a=
nd left that in previous years seemed like given wins for Republicans. Gove=
rnors=E2=80=99 mansions across the country likewise lit up blue as Democrat=
s ascended even in the reddest of states, such as Texas.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Voters <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial=
.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECyyyKi=
IcsbT_mvO_CmKOtXJ9Vuc5GUeszmf0ONAjnAzaSzNPI2rLOa7NW0Um9xg8L_xvGfYFY1NX5z5I7=
PHx-W80BhA565_gC0ASJFv-gZFfKKXmih4JPzTuEC1CHZeGOvqYWv_7tb_HUYungEt6SfQAifNT=
3Rzl0OKRD7blK4lxzPxEx95myX0V3qdLCkdQRXw5EUOPXVdsNDOOnhSJ2aCz9aQq6h6kGBV8TkO=
V1JxUAVaA9CIdKqpdKPyKpyZ80/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h19/h001.GxMrHDXTaicT=
WGVXhdr1u4HGgp1Zdv8qOFm1SDvjGeA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">concerned about =
corruption</a> expressed their displeasure at oligarchs=E2=80=99 blatant at=
tempts to create a political environment to their liking. Voting against te=
chnocrats drove people into the hands of Democrats and away from Republican=
s. Tech oligarchs themselves, along with anger over the AI boom, datacenter=
s and Flock surveillance cameras, shifted the tides.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CVoters rejected Republicans in pa=
rt because they were bought and paid for by AI billionaires. Democrats must=
 hold them accountable instead of cashing their checks,=E2=80=9D <a href=3D=
"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.wtfWA9uPAn8i7Lb0U_hU2gO=
xBa96QNNgm0dysd1DLp1q_GDCcxCWUmToYu53JeoC5jw99v-XIYC8RX1v-Msu-mvkiUrbCVTN-j=
AREVnmU0of036td0_cfdBWVUdhBFM9q8nI4GcBHuvg3GWK41wGAPNpS3DTO4oGSBBIbCsR7CWqv=
knsilasDWVkBP5ivhwTflNQMuZuyWMjYAOwepMutazuhuLB_5Zpd5NE4D0SIJzjUbq0NZxkV14Y=
_tyjJkUxUR0K5Pl5_-jeJ46xlP77EA2xiwR-rD6iv_dlEND9MEc/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQK=
QUQ/h20/h001.M69N1_zd-UBWD9f4Hz8ZNb1qvKULwAKd_Z4PkPDF4FY" style=3D"color: #=
0077B6;">wrote</a> Texas Democratic representative Greg Casar.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Georgia Democrat Jon Ossoff, who won re-el=
ection to the Senate, summed up the prevailing attitude towards the tech in=
dustry in his victory speech.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CThe titans of Silicon Valley dig =
bunkers for themselves and warn that the artificial intelligence they=E2=80=
=99re creating risks human extinction,=E2=80=9D he said. He pledged to brin=
g =E2=80=9Cbig tech to heel=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Others were more bellicose. Ed Markey, a D=
emocratic senator from Massachusetts, <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.t=
heguardian.com/ss/c/u001.QvkQtXiSzSINXrMyEJiuYt0OYpDDTT613UNh6Wrlp1iPdNcR3S=
_RnD-w2S6HCJ21cskvhkbIkl3CVjWUYQjmB7kNBes25XtTnKaBZW_rP81KXgGcqcDJoT0tRam5B=
zk-jUOO-BTx_DBHSYOnLjv56K_AIksEt9X7AI0M_WEJSugmOAlxYeZ4ZqoS1J-yYoFA-BARtQCA=
rYLlZLVC0te76hYGr8Jm_gTPLHD0vgTx-l4C9wscdW1bB98OVl4eYrdf/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjla=
TSyQKQUQ/h21/h001.tHj4oMeO29R0NDKNb0VhcEynpqYxOfuovFGYF_eoa64" style=3D"col=
or: #0077B6;">tweeted</a> late on Tuesday: =E2=80=9CThey are going to need =
to plant new forests for all of the subpoenas we=E2=80=99ll be printing.=E2=
=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Democrats have both promised congressional=
 investigations into tech companies and moratoriums on datacenters, which m=
ay hamstring compute-hungry AI companies.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In the past year, the major AI firms have =
been competing in a fierce race to buy or build massive, noisy, resource-in=
tensive facilities full of semiconductor chips that will supply their growi=
ng needs for computing power. Americans <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial=
.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRz9kx0yV4F7mbSmcsLjidBIiNvq8=
j_-vVlC5bsuD9Df8gcHCxoXT861sCVDv2LB0S-p0uDz7UoD9BqzHm3JjuiUu7i95wRXqKOLfUSO=
1R0S5voVMIeg8X_ww5Xy45xkoSaVdASnl1aiOVU35SXILAHrJkwBkKJnpEVvLfFCB6SNAJBmQWa=
WxdqqHifo51t5rjRlzrIjy72EbzxXVhxMkCdDXbvgRn7Rf5eRm4QAaQiY-evO3-Ds-sauE8sJ4F=
y3Rmg/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h22/h001.-f26U55QjdcQGrIRQLoUe00RRQPBMaimX=
n_ixeYL1Do" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">hate them</a>. Democrats stand firmly=
 in the way of that arms race. Democrats took governors=E2=80=99 mansions b=
y promising to institute moratoriums on hyperscale datacenter construction.=
</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Gina Hinojosa of Texas, Amy Acton of Ohio,=
 and Keisha Lance Bottoms of Georgia have <a href=3D"https://ablink.editori=
al.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR_aJBDmowNoWoDOyBvi6Tv6s1O=
PYje84tOVAkHayEn_oZiqVAvOsG2LFxKL8OpzBsEKYLtq4QaR9LkSdkr5sm4LoIb3d9-HGxMj0s=
j9M28g_FQFMz81tP8aYy00V5TJgihdCu_gXhX7IYBibakpXvorBPxaY6oin7n4LHqKXaZBFLNx_=
XdCe4tgWgY3TMeLGdLjA8Bzlbi5QXPdWkMpa1vbyi4iy4wJ2cc0e9LXZiQT92PZsnor2wRTPDoc=
h3vrSnQ/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h23/h001.sApJKrWnlymiRA6k0h19lucN4OP8NAv=
RGoAs7G9NnTg" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">all pledged pauses</a>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Then there are the promised investigations=
. Letters to preserve records for future investigations <a href=3D"https://=
ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR0JRNkgBBrBs=
aFz1BS69vPSjpBOwFbpPzOQrXWgmFU9V-lrjcx_VdqENe6uFj-63dtTkz9ju13XSAxxNr3FkoXs=
UCSMg0Qui_krfAcTM23uCxu_ROL-C9EJhC-olNTyV1qYv-ViLZRvm_xqwWWFBpxve65smlfMyXi=
j2DqSeLx6DUoEorauAACmU60u6rhwzfkUhvf-Isdb9m0-s3iwyujHZhd3wdWeq2ymi6xVEl4stc=
rI2Ysj6pC9eVvupMmT0UoTSo3NSbuwceNZBBZS-Cdw1_bGCXxAnGCaH1RwLR5uU/4vh/KApF2FN=
fQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h24/h001.0ucCnt-UZp1-hXU76izWEq7-ylugEx8XLSPO6RRlus4" style=
=3D"color: #0077B6;">have already gone out</a> to Nvidia and Amazon. Tech w=
as the <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkL=
MEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDUZSC8KPzZutimV4n8d8SzAO5gN4X-eUBZyF_X0=
0JNUSwwGTCAziBveQCCYTHhJZBef8YJKC0-dER2Xvdsq4OTIU2fjxnJH9kxfjf6Kmi8SGwKxRPa=
ePLsPHEizcm0zusbfvoqSo1mXznIl8gNMX5pKd5_npV2HoRZE7rnEEsef5ta1eug6scoAfdDqss=
7SrCpbXyac9nHSbumaQQ9PqVRqApVwPTBHYxt00t4RO8FzEUuAMa6b0ow6_22jD8Y5zs/4vh/KA=
pF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h25/h001.w85jQi_l4wQD3BOoUkbn1Fv8ZTk4U4Cq8lo7LsvBFIA" =
style=3D"color: #0077B6;">villain of the midterms</a>. Angry constituents w=
ant to see it penalized. Elon Musk presents a meaty target as the billionai=
re most closely allied with the Trump administration and the richest man in=
 the world. Investigating his conduct with the =E2=80=9Cdepartment of gover=
nment efficiency=E2=80=9D, which laid waste to the humanitarian agency USAI=
D and wide swaths of the US government, will be a political lay-up for Demo=
crats newly in control and desiring a public spectacle.</p>
