ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Musk had the worst night of anyone but Tru=
mp on Tuesday. The world=E2=80=99s richest man gave $450m in support of Rep=
ublican candidates, most of all to Ken Paxton in Texas, but he reaped littl=
e, if any, reward. Paxton lost by a major margin. Musk remained silent for =
some eight hours as results poured in, each piece of news more disastrous f=
or his right-wing project than the last. In what seemed like capitulation, =
he deleted a Tuesday tweet that read: =E2=80=9CVote red today!=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">By Wednesday morning, the SpaceX CEO wante=
d off the planet. =E2=80=9CDatacenters in space are looking pretty good rig=
ht now,=E2=80=9D he wrote.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">He may not get the chance to set up his or=
bital computers. Democrats may likewise investigate or attempt to unwind th=
e multibillion dollar merger of SpaceX and Musk=E2=80=99s AI company, xAI, =
which makes the <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u0=
01.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEA13-uHzzNLsl3ZqJFCJlFe-BNrU_7z=
ZD8HFI0adJcSsH8MXylsKbeJ7ld-IKiH-1i7umiiyVblqDdUnC1Hj0HJ0yrtU3qgTHUeOhjU8Kd=
vOwH_4p3TC31fYBT2SSG-uH72CE2_37d1wxAgwFl-Ibr5hgF8qyoMXETgunaTai4rza1FtKuwtO=
lCC329FykOrF_cqu8BrB1YYSLKv3KSPTWim0xB15sPBKrT7geY0LkIIj5drZarpV-HfaIJ2sxii=
nQ/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h26/h001.tM0cyTNqAm2tzLJEpPPhRMl8XIeCY-Y6YhYv=
DFCIRYA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Nazi-friendly</a> <a href=3D"https://abl=
ink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgsz=
cCSneHEA13-uHzzNLsl3ZqJFCJlFeVQeeppDwDpuabThgS3oG4T7PNmhU07aRyoJ5J36Lub2tGp=
GvP57wzVujzmSeug-oIU1Q3CgNBBXoz11od9t7BlmR0p_WWxF29b3maLS9YK-hq11RSYGjKaHca=
2ho8FrUsrVZt-AGUDQ4-2q_Zf4MQ-HKraGJdiLevvFmoKd4_0KJMHZ10gGrPZZezLV7IMnwKNN9=
AGGDpDVy5hnXQpLeTsRsaXgp8shfW9jkEAh_qtE/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h27/h001=
.v-aet_qO60eGXGbPu9M7jDaMbxhwv3itOTK05oulzEE" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">nud=
ification</a> bot Grok. xAI has a $200m contract with the US military, whic=
h likewise seems like an easy win for Democrats to meddle with.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Mark Zuckerberg may feel deja vu when he f=
inds himself sitting across the table from an inquisition, as he repeatedly=
 did at the end of the 2010s. The Meta CEO made a nakedly political pivot u=
nder Trump 2.0 with his shift to the right. He appeared at Mar-a-Lago to sh=
ow off Meta=E2=80=99s camera-equipped glasses to Trump and <a href=3D"https=
://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7f=
IEMgszcCSneHEDemkX49beNf88r4VT8N5woecvNdfgmoHoCFYqs1M2zEDwUxG9RwkwhEzzDRH4A=
yz8aCkFB_94vW_uncikEtd8N4I6SoVmbKwW26oI2_ffZ-vabrpzwZsmWnrskWidBIPoMhbKoWt5=
_h19PK7SbXLNcJO16l0ldUditn9yFeK76989XqcC-OVhKDTWmssAeYpc82JIaY71SJ-3xhNoRcN=
UJfr2OVJ00eMIhpYuPygzKuA/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h28/h001.yZDY_wVaPbtYay=
SK3K57El-TSDQOfNQGdpn7HIcmIxc" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">axed his company=
=E2=80=99s vaunted diversity, equity, and inclusion program</a> as the pres=
ident waged war on DEI.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Already the most disliked man in America, =
Zuckerberg will show with his next era whether he believes in anything as m=
uch as he does power. Was his interest in jiu-jitsu mixed martial arts auth=
entic or a way to ingratiate himself with the <a href=3D"https://ablink.edi=
torial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHE=
DemkX49beNf88r4VT8N5woecvNdfgmoHoCFYqs1M2zEDO2VsNE_HdxFpOtYvq-lzi_3Il_nlQB6=
t2-PfKjLbGwjw_KChhFZELl20T9Yv-sUp5b4MfDncQWVV4UUQGM6vXeyWC_VR-5_47odPtghYza=
H-fk0-Lm9lU4ViPIDpaHngBgUbrMzwKZmuP2cfLIzsxZD96zUNKWxaY06PJxdaDDufRBxPieVEQ=
oj5QDfRJv8DEeBoEd1ZyXraRPQx5ANriMVUr-u6cFzlXIgDM6lpr6ShCtfd9FcftjLSehoMQiqg=
/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h29/h001.zUMwKyLe2azN1ljLbW8dRDzAXaQvNcXyLnaBn9=
NCGVI" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">manosphere=E2=80=99s</a> podcast hosts? We=
 may know by the time he faces his first inquest. Perhaps he=E2=80=99ll ret=
urn to the liberal roots of his former public image like founding a <a href=
=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18I=
R0JRNkgBBrBsaFz1BS69vPSjpBOwFbpPzOQrXWgmFU9V4TtQrYk4XW_Guc5KRQ1f-RaTd9OEyNR=
kfMR_9SzajmmWTfCPI9AWen1PxKktVeCHAuWvPHcX6RPWyMFkwBd51Cuuj53So8l_E-_uAT2Spj=
TZgwM8o6l8YSBf1EJ8yGSONOHZOPt7kslgSrgwjZqlx7SD1_7n8iVuUb7E_jsddXS7X1AVnFOrT=
NmblwPz3x_kTsy5kp3gQ4odSs0dL-WpFG1N6luLL76fy986EY-1CPtvWdB1QUVc1BrWJwiv5DJe=
3w8akvgLune-7MrWF8j7QA/4vh/KApF2FNfQTGjlaTSyQKQUQ/h30/h001.FGVTDcfaTzNUSlCS=
27IaOSvpGCCiCo4ckX6kYnr2tlg" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">pro-immigration nonp=
rofit</a>, as he did a decade ago.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Meanwhile, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman, himself =
seen at Mar-a-Lago, appears in damage control mode on Tuesday. His tweet on=
 Tuesday night read like a Bernie Sanders talking point: =E2=80=9CPeople sh=
ould not cede control of the future to superintelligence, and that requirem=
ent should ultimately constrain AI progress.=E2=80=9D Inviting human-first =
regulation, Altman appeared to be trying to distance himself from Trump=E2=
=80=99s free-for-all stance, and the president=E2=80=99s recent efforts to =
rebrand AI as =E2=80=9Csuperintelligence=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">But the billionaires of Silicon Valley see=
m unlikely to rehabilitate their public images overnight after years of pan=
dering only to power brokers. They have little to say on the issues of the =
day: affordability and corruption. The majority of Americans see them as av=
atars of extreme wealth inequality and cynical, pay-to-play politics. What =
can a billionaire offer a populace angry about prices?</p>
